                <pb facs="0132" n="62" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg62"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3583: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sevier</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-03T12:00:00-04:00">March 3,
                        1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 12:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. My telegram No. 26, February 28, 6 p.m. The Foreign Minister and principal
                    Foreign Office officials have left the city for the weekend. <pb facs="0133"
                        n="63" xml:id="pg63"/> It is understood that no action by Chile in regard to
                    Paraguay’s rejection of the League formula will be considered prior to early
                    part of next week.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sevier</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
